---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { buttonVariants } from '../components/ui/button';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ';
const schema = {'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'SoftwareApplication',name:'Ticker',url:'https://ticker.megabyte.sh',operatingSystem:'macOS 26 or newer; Apple Silicon',applicationCategory:'UtilitiesApplication',description:'A native macOS menu bar crypto ticker with a customizable watchlist, USD prices and 1-hour, 24-hour and 1-week percentage changes.',downloadUrl:'https://ticker.megabyte.sh/downloads/Ticker-1.0-arm64.dmg',softwareVersion:'1.0',offers:{'@type':'Offer',price:'0',priceCurrency:'USD'}};
---
<Layout title="Ticker: crypto prices in your Mac menu bar" description="Track Bitcoin, Ethereum and your crypto watchlist in the macOS menu bar. Native SwiftUI, no account or API key. Free Apple Silicon DMG for macOS 26+." schema={schema}>
<section class="hero wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">Native macOS crypto ticker</p><h1>Keep a price<br/>in sight.</h1><p class="hero-copy">Bitcoin, Ethereum and your watchlist. One click away, in your Mac menu bar.</p><div class="actions"><a href="/downloads/Ticker-1.0-arm64.dmg" download class={buttonVariants({className:"large-button"})}>Download Ticker</a><a class="text-link" href="/download/">Installation details ↗</a></div></div><figure class="product-visual"><img class="native-preview" src="/ticker-native.png" width="640" height="590" alt="Ticker's native macOS popup, with stars on the left, token symbols above names, USD prices and the change-period selector." fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption class="preview-caption">Native Ticker interface. Prices shown at capture time.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="requirements wrap"><span>macOS 26+</span><span>Apple Silicon</span><span>Free download</span><a href="/download/#security">Ad-hoc signed release ↗</a></section>
<section class="feature-section wrap"><div><h2>A watchlist.<br/>Without another tab.</h2><p>Add the tokens you follow. Star one to put its USD price in the menu bar. Your choices stay saved between launches.</p></div><dl class="feature-list"><div><dt>Choose your time frame</dt><dd>Switch between 1-hour, 24-hour and 1-week percentage changes in the same popup.</dd></div><div><dt>Search by name or symbol</dt><dd>Press ⌘N or click + to find tokens on CoinGecko. Escape returns to your watchlist.</dd></div><div><dt>Know when data is stale</dt><dd>Prices refresh every minute. Ticker labels outdated data when the service cannot provide a fresh quote.</dd></div></dl></section>
<section class="steps-section wrap"><h2>From download to menu bar.</h2><ol class="steps"><li><span>01</span><h3>Move it to Applications</h3><p>Open the DMG and drag Ticker into Applications.</p></li><li><span>02</span><h3>Open Ticker</h3><p>Follow the <a href="/download/#security">security instructions</a> for this release, then look in the menu bar.</p></li><li><span>03</span><h3>Make it yours</h3><p>Add a token. Click its star. That price stays in sight.</p></li></ol></section>
<section class="guide-section wrap"><h2>Before you pick a ticker.</h2><p>Practical notes on menu bar apps, price data and choosing the right tool.</p><div class="guide-links"><a href="/guides/mac-crypto-ticker-alternatives/"><span>Comparison</span><h3>Crypto tickers for Mac: what to compare</h3><p>Ticker, Coin Tick and Crypto Pro serve different needs.</p></a><a href="/guides/bitcoin-price-mac-menu-bar/"><span>Setup</span><h3>Put Bitcoin in your Mac menu bar</h3><p>A short setup guide, including what the displayed price means.</p></a><a href="/guides/crypto-price-refresh-stale-data/"><span>Price data</span><h3>Why your crypto ticker can show an old price</h3><p>Refresh intervals, rate limits and stale data.</p></a></div></section>
<section class="faq-section wrap"><h2>A few details.</h2><FAQ client:visible/><p class="fine">Looking for alerts, trading or portfolio totals? <a href="/guides/mac-crypto-ticker-alternatives/">Compare alternatives</a> before installing.</p></section>
</Layout>
